# --- s043 Book I d.12 q.2 (two spirators)
n("n720","s043-01","Secunda questio duodecime distinctionis","la","source","The question whether Father and Son are *duo spirantes* or *duo spiratores* is not a separate question in Scotus's *Ordinatio* I d. 12 as edited (Vat. V has qq. 1–2). Gorris may take it from the *Reportatio* or from Scotus's discussion in d. 12. B also has a separate question here. The Scotist source is to be identified.","to-verify")
n("n721","s043-02","q. 35. articulo vltimo","la","source","Aquinas, *ST* I q. 36 a. 4 ad 7 (the last article of q. 36): *duo spirantes… non tamen duo spiratores, propter unam spirationem*. A's *q. 35* is apparently an error for *q. 36*. The same slip occurs at 046 (*q. 35 a. 2*); compare *q. 41* for q. 42 at 045.","to-verify")
n("n722","s043-03","nullum nomen verbale","la","source","The grammatical doctrine of the *nomen verbale* (agent noun) signifying *per modum habitus et quietis*, as against the participle signifying *per modum fluxus*, from modistic grammar. Scotus applies it to *spirator/spirans*.","to-verify")
n("n723","s043-03","cuiusdam noui doctoris","la","historical","‘A certain new doctor’. The person is not identified. The phrase marks a recent author, distinct from *doctor* (Scotus) used in the same paragraph.","uncertain")
n("n724","s043-01","two spirating","en","translation","*duo spirantes* (participle) is rendered ‘two spirating’ throughout, to keep the grammatical point against *duo spiratores* (agent noun).")

# --- B collation (full): B61L–B62L
upd("n721", append=" B also *q. 35. ar. vl.*.")
n("n983","s043-02","Quare terminus numeralis","la","textual","B: *quare materialis terminus*, and again *terminus materialis appositus* in 03, a misreading of *numeralis* that destroys the argument.","certain")
